e9996d"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":158624,"output_tokens":5417,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion that structurally parses docker-compose.yml to assert the mcp service sets the fail-closed REBAR_MCP_* env (transport=http, AUTH_ENABLED=1, TLS_AT_EDGE=true, allowlist) and loopback 127.0.0.1:8091, and that Dockerfile.mcp builds rebar-mcp with the shared base.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope enumerates env: REBAR_MCP_TRANSPORT=http ... REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ENABLED=1 etc and a container HEALTHCHECK","ACs cover /health gauge, fail-closed build_server gate, nginx upstream, SIGTERM — none parse docker-compose.yml env or Dockerfile.mcp","AC4 only ties stop_grace_period to the module constant"],"finding":"The compose service and Dockerfile.mcp are described deliverables (fail-closed env vars, loopback publish, restart:always, container HEALTHCHECK, MCP_PATHS comment) but no acceptance criterion structurally verifies them; AC2 asserts the _resolve_http_runtime gates in code, not that docker-compose.yml actually sets REBAR_MCP_* to the fail-closed values or that Dockerfile.mcp builds rebar-mcp.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbc0c70a58b87415c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria / Scope (docker-compose.yml, Dockerfile.mcp)","norm_id":"ne2ed352cdd26f7fa","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Extend the structural-parse AC to cover the compose env block and Dockerfile CMD/HEALTHCHECK, not just the nginx template.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the SIGTERM gauge-gated drain (DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS=1200 / stop_grace_period 1260s) with ADR-0104 §2, which rejects the review-bot stop-and-drain for MCP in favor of blue-green retire-when-idle; justify why a drain is still needed here or drop it in favor of the ADR's decoupled-retirement model.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ADR-0104 §2 (docs/adr/0104-mcp-on-box.md:59-81): 'The MCP autodeploy target does not copy the review-bot's stop-and-health-drain' and 'a gauge-gated drain bound would then be exhausted and kill an in-flight certified op... merely enlarging the bound only defers the same kill. Blue-green decouples retirement from the deploy'","ADR-0104:85-87: 'A killed MCP op is client-visible ... and rebar's event-sourced writes are idempotent ... so retirement is safe' — i.e. a long SIGTERM drain is not required for correctness","The plan cites this same ADR as its authority ('per ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur')"],"finding":"The plan's new SIGTERM gauge-gated drain (DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS=1200 in _mcp_health.py, waiting for in_flight to reach 0 before exit, covered by stop_grace_period: 1260s) rebuilds the exact review-bot stop-and-drain pattern that the governing ADR-0104 §2 EXPLICITLY REJECTS for the MCP target.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f99df1ff2149e0266","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan sections 'SIGTERM grace (concrete numbers)' and Scope bullet 'bounded SIGTERM grace so a retiring container lets an in-flight op finish'","norm_id":"nf04920b354fc61a3","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A shared MCP server driven by N agents pipelines long LLM ops so in_flight may never reach 0; the 1200s SIGTERM drain then exhausts and Docker SIGKILLs mid-op — the precise failure ADR-0104 designed blue-green to avoid.","A reviewer/implementer follows the ADR's blue-green retire-when-idle model in foxterrier while this plan simultaneously ships a conflicting stop-and-drain grace, producing two contradictory retirement mechanisms."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{